WEBVTT

00:02.080 --> 00:04.498
- Hi, I'm Brian Griffin.
- I'm Stewart.

00:04.582 --> 00:08.336
Many of you have written in
with suggestions for episodes.

00:08.336 --> 00:11.796
They're mostly God-awful.

00:11.879 --> 00:15.216
Well, we've produced
three of our favourite suggestions.

00:15.341 --> 00:17.302
Favourites? That's charitable.

00:17.427 --> 00:19.510
What is that?

00:19.594 --> 00:22.847
- It's from Dharma and Greg.
- I'm surprised it still works.

00:22.930 --> 00:25.350
- Whoa!
- Enjoy.

00:25.433 --> 00:29.187
"It seems today that all you see

00:29.312 --> 00:32.521
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:32.646 --> 00:36.275
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:36.275 --> 00:39.319
"On which we used to rely?

00:39.403 --> 00:42.531
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:42.656 --> 00:47.535
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:47.660 --> 00:49.202
"Laugh and cry

00:49.327 --> 00:54.540
"He's a family guy

01:04.339 --> 01:06.717
Now back to "The Newlywed Game".

01:06.841 --> 01:09.761
Carol, how did Nick answer the following:

01:09.845 --> 01:13.097
"The last thing I would ever
give my wife is... blank"?

01:13.180 --> 01:15.475
A little spending money?

01:15.807 --> 01:18.727
Sorry, that's incorrect. Nick actually said

01:18.811 --> 01:20.269
"the antidote".

01:20.269 --> 01:24.441
- Nick, what are you talking abou...?
- Oh, Meg, you were right.

01:26.943 --> 01:30.904
- Oh, my God! A genie!
- I am here to grant you three wishes.

01:31.029 --> 01:35.490
- Peter, three wishes! This is so exciting!
- I want a new hat!

01:35.615 --> 01:38.117
- I want a new hat!
- I want them to have new hats!

01:38.200 --> 01:41.871
Kids, these are your father's wishes.
Get whatever you want.

01:41.955 --> 01:45.832
That's easy. I wish I could see
what Kelly Ripa was like off the set.

01:45.916 --> 01:48.001
So it shall be.

01:49.252 --> 01:51.754
- Great show today, Kelly.
- Thanks. You, too.

01:58.009 --> 02:00.845
Gelman needs us onstage
for a couple of reshoots.

02:00.929 --> 02:03.432
Be right there. I have to put on my face.

02:04.181 --> 02:07.100
Did you see the size of that dressing room?

02:07.183 --> 02:10.019
- They must really want to keep her.
- Your second wish?

02:10.103 --> 02:13.981
I gotjust the thing.
I wish I had my own theme music.

02:14.065 --> 02:15.441
Done!

02:18.651 --> 02:21.571
- I don't hear anything.
- Get up. Try it out.

02:30.037 --> 02:31.496
Sweet!

03:01.521 --> 03:03.605
Yeah-yeah-yeah-yeah!

03:10.152 --> 03:12.154
Hey, wanna turn that stuff down?

03:12.237 --> 03:15.991
Come on, that's classic travelling music.
Try to enjoy it.

03:16.116 --> 03:18.826
"Riding on a bus, riding on a bus,
sitting next to bums

03:18.910 --> 03:20.702
"There's an open seat, hope that isn't pee

03:20.786 --> 03:24.540
- I'm sick of hearing it!
- I'm sorry, buddy, I can't turn it off.

03:24.665 --> 03:27.459
Then I'm gonna break
every bone in your body.

03:27.584 --> 03:30.378
- I wish I had no bones!
- Done.

03:31.754 --> 03:33.006
That ought to show you!

03:38.218 --> 03:43.222
Oh, no. I gotta fart,
but I don't know which way to lean.

03:45.307 --> 03:49.142
I know you might be a little concerned
about me not having bones,

03:49.142 --> 03:51.438
but I gotta tell you, it's not that bad.

03:51.563 --> 03:53.648
Dad's just like Silly Putty.

03:53.731 --> 03:57.483
Look what I can do to Mary Worth's
smug sense of self-satisfaction.

03:57.608 --> 04:00.528
That's right, son. Take her down a peg.

04:00.612 --> 04:03.322
I guess we could all adjust to this.

04:03.322 --> 04:07.075
- Look! I'm making an angel!
- See? Everything's gonna be fine.

04:07.075 --> 04:09.702
Now smile while I write
my name in you.

04:15.123 --> 04:17.209
Argh! Argh!

04:18.459 --> 04:19.710
Let go!

04:24.589 --> 04:25.549
Aagh!

04:34.389 --> 04:36.806
But, Mom, I've got to
use the bathroom now!

04:36.891 --> 04:40.561
Your father gets incredibly filthy
rolling around everywhere.

04:40.644 --> 04:44.522
- He has to take 12 baths a day.
- I don't like Dad any more.

04:44.605 --> 04:47.733
I invited some friends over
to jump on him like a trampoline,

04:47.733 --> 04:50.569
but his roll of fat sucked up Ryan's shoe

04:50.652 --> 04:52.654
and his mom yelled at him
when he got home

04:52.738 --> 04:56.825
and he beat me up at school the next day!
It's all here in this pamphlet.

04:56.908 --> 05:01.078
We have to learn to accept this,
like one of those stories on Dateline

05:01.203 --> 05:06.291
where a family member suffers a horrible
accident and is a burden on everybody.

05:06.416 --> 05:10.460
They pretend to be happy,
but they're dead inside. They're dead.

05:10.585 --> 05:12.754
And that'll be our lives, hm?

05:12.879 --> 05:15.465
What a big, boneless jerk I am.

05:15.590 --> 05:19.968
I might've screwed up my life but there's
no reason to keep screwing up theirs.

05:20.052 --> 05:22.763
Goodbye, cruel bone-filled world!

05:30.060 --> 05:33.814
Oh, so this is where
all the waste and sewage winds up.

05:37.984 --> 05:40.193
Aaaargh!

05:40.277 --> 05:43.738
Cut and print. That's a wrap.
Greatjob, Peter.

05:43.822 --> 05:46.324
- Coming to the wrap party?
- I don't know.

05:46.450 --> 05:49.784
I got a stand-up comedy class
at The Learning Annex.

05:49.868 --> 05:54.664
Actually, I won't be a stand-up comic.
I'll be more like an amorphous-blob comic.

05:54.790 --> 05:56.874
- I gotta write that down.
- Nonsense!

05:56.958 --> 06:00.627
I'll have the studio send a flatbed for you!
See you at eight!

06:09.802 --> 06:12.512
There's something
I've wanted to say all evening.

06:12.596 --> 06:15.223
What's that,
Mrs Catherine Zeta-Jones Douglas?

06:15.306 --> 06:19.392
- I want to jump your non-bones.
- Jeez, I can't believe I'm your type.

06:19.476 --> 06:23.563
As you can tell from my husband,
I've got a thing for saggy, shapeless men.

06:23.646 --> 06:27.316
I'm married to Catherine Zeta-Jones.
Will you sleep with me?

06:27.400 --> 06:28.859
I'll have to pass.

06:28.983 --> 06:34.488
But Louie Anderson's eating the decorative
soaps in the bathroom. Why not try him?

06:34.613 --> 06:38.868
- Aren't you Peter, the human stunt bag?
- That depends on who's asking.

06:38.993 --> 06:42.954
I'm a doctor doing an experimental procedure
to give bones to ajellyfish,

06:43.037 --> 06:45.540
but I'd like to try it on a human. Interested?

06:45.540 --> 06:47.332
- I don't know.
- Interested?

06:47.415 --> 06:49.710
Didn't you just say that? I'll do it!

06:51.794 --> 06:55.672
The operation was a complete success!
What are you going to do now?

06:55.755 --> 06:59.425
I had the operation
so I could go back to my family.

06:59.509 --> 07:02.220
It's been so long.
What if they don't love me any more?

07:02.220 --> 07:05.139
Where do you think
all those bones came from?

07:05.139 --> 07:07.141
- Surprise!
- My God!

07:07.224 --> 07:10.269
You mean it's your bones that are inside me?

07:10.352 --> 07:13.062
Mostly. We picked up
a drifter to fill in the torso.

07:13.187 --> 07:17.649
Like I always say, a family of freaks
is better than no family at all!

07:17.649 --> 07:22.778
Let's go home! You know what's weird?
This was covered by my HMO.

07:35.789 --> 07:38.500
You dare me to pop a wheelie in this thing?

07:38.500 --> 07:41.335
That doesn't sound safe at all.
OK, I dare you.

07:45.380 --> 07:47.467
Wow! That was great!

07:52.803 --> 07:55.306
Six! Six bats.

07:55.390 --> 07:58.016
Seven! Seven bats!

07:59.142 --> 08:01.352
- Is the Count a vampire?
- What's that?

08:01.436 --> 08:06.564
Those big fangs. Have they ever shown him
do somebody in, then feed on him?

08:06.647 --> 08:09.066
You're asking if they've
done a Sesame Street

08:09.150 --> 08:13.028
in which the Count kills somebody,
then sucks their blood for sustenance?

08:13.112 --> 08:14.572
- Yeah.
- No.

08:14.697 --> 08:16.781
There's something out in the yard!

08:18.743 --> 08:23.747
- It looks like the back of a tanker truck.
- Wow! What do you think's inside?

08:23.872 --> 08:25.747
- Maybe it's candy!
- Chris, no!

08:25.831 --> 08:28.250
Lois, Lois. Let him dream.

08:31.377 --> 08:34.797
- Eugh! What is this stuff?
- It's some kind of nuclear waste.

08:34.921 --> 08:38.048
Dear me.
Does anyone else feel a trifle queasy?

08:39.175 --> 08:41.594
What? Do I have a boogie? I say!

08:41.678 --> 08:44.806
It appears my cranium has doubled in size!

08:48.140 --> 08:53.062
How delightful! This toxic stew seems
to have given me telekinetic abilities!

08:57.649 --> 08:59.733
Hey! I can make fire!

08:59.817 --> 09:02.945
Come here a second.
This is gonna be hilarious.

09:02.945 --> 09:07.741
OK, on the count of three. One, two, three...

09:09.324 --> 09:10.451
Do it again!

09:13.078 --> 09:16.831
All right. Clearly something
very strange has happened here.

09:16.915 --> 09:20.168
We've each acquired superpowers
from that nuclear waste.

09:20.251 --> 09:24.630
We've been given a gift.
Whether that gift is Chris's fire conjuring,

09:24.754 --> 09:27.966
Stewie's telekinesis, Brian's superspeed...

09:28.091 --> 09:30.050
- Ask how the queen of England is.
- How's...

09:30.176 --> 09:33.178
- She's great.
... Peter's morphing ability...

09:33.178 --> 09:35.679
Hey, Lois, I'm a wishing troll.

09:36.639 --> 09:39.350
...my superstrength,

09:39.434 --> 09:44.437
or Meg's, um... super-amazing
ability to grow her fingernails,

09:46.439 --> 09:51.318
we must to use these powers properly
and not abuse them for personal gain.

09:51.443 --> 09:52.486
- Understand?
- Yes.

09:52.570 --> 09:54.362
- Mm-hm.
- Got it.

09:58.199 --> 10:02.911
Oh, no. I forgot the detergent. Excuse me,
would you watch him for a moment?

10:02.994 --> 10:04.871
Sure thing, ma'am.

10:04.997 --> 10:07.164
Whoa there, little guy. You gotta pay for that.

10:07.289 --> 10:09.583
Go suck a railroad spike. I have no money.

10:09.666 --> 10:13.420
Then I'm afraid I'm gonna
have to take it away from you.

10:13.545 --> 10:16.047
Argh! Argh! Argh!

10:16.130 --> 10:18.966
Oh, God! Please help me!

10:22.094 --> 10:25.012
Move it, you slowpoke, the light's green!

10:25.095 --> 10:30.226
What does that cloud look like to you,
honey? To me it looks like... rain.

10:30.308 --> 10:33.352
I used thatjoke at work today.
I'm the funniest guy at the office.

10:33.435 --> 10:37.190
- They say I should do stand-up.
- Oh! This is insane!

10:46.572 --> 10:50.242
Oh, my God, *NSync is in town.
If you get me a lock of Justin's hair,

10:50.326 --> 10:53.870
I'll never ask you
for shopping money again. Please?!

10:53.870 --> 10:57.122
We promised Lois
we'd use our powers responsibly.

10:57.206 --> 11:00.125
I suppose doing the exact opposite
couldn't hurt.

11:05.254 --> 11:10.342
- Hey, do you want to split a Toblerone?
- Oh, gosh! Yeah. I think I do.

11:10.467 --> 11:13.262
Whoo-whoo! Next stop, my thighs!

11:14.929 --> 11:17.765
All right, Meg, wait here. I'll be right back.

11:18.056 --> 11:20.558
Hi. Britney Spears. You mind if I go in?

11:20.683 --> 11:23.603
- Oh, not at all, Miss Spears.
- Oh, call me Peter.

11:23.686 --> 11:26.731
- Hey, fellas.
- Britney? What are you doing here?

11:26.813 --> 11:30.568
I was in the neighbourhood -
I'm gonna steal one of your beers -

11:30.692 --> 11:32.986
and I figured I'd stop by and say hi.

11:33.070 --> 11:35.071
You mind if I have a seat?

11:36.614 --> 11:40.366
- I am out of shape. I got a favour to ask you.
- What is it?

11:40.492 --> 11:43.204
I got a hole in my car's muffler.
I need to plug it.

11:43.287 --> 11:45.579
- Can I have some of your hair?
- I guess so.

11:45.705 --> 11:49.750
Oh, great. Thanks. All right, hold still now.

11:50.918 --> 11:53.295
You'll be fine. Give me a kiss.

11:54.962 --> 11:59.258
- Agh!
- I'm Gene Shalit now! Bye!

12:01.343 --> 12:03.427
- Here's your martini.
- Thanks.

12:03.511 --> 12:07.264
- Hey, it's gone!
- I'm sorry, ma'am. Here's another one.

12:07.388 --> 12:09.684
What the hell is going on here?

12:11.642 --> 12:15.938
Hi. Can I get some pretzels or something?
I gotta drive.

12:16.021 --> 12:20.317
Hey, did you bring enough breasts
for the rest of the class?

12:24.362 --> 12:26.989
Hector, how long have we known each other?

12:27.072 --> 12:29.365
- Since first grade.
- Yeah. Yeah.

12:29.491 --> 12:32.619
You remember that time
you called me "Chris Gristle"?

12:32.702 --> 12:35.538
- I think so.
- Well, burn for it!

12:41.251 --> 12:45.129
It's a bird, it's a plane,
it's a lower-middle-class Irish family.

12:45.212 --> 12:48.256
This is just one of
many public disturbances

12:48.340 --> 12:52.635
caused by the Griffin family of Quahog,
who seem to have acquired superpowers.

12:52.719 --> 12:56.179
Very strange story, Diane.
Coming up next: Can bees think?

12:56.263 --> 12:58.974
A new study confirms that no, they cannot.

13:00.975 --> 13:03.353
Citizens of Quahog, we have a problem!

13:03.478 --> 13:05.771
You're damn right! Peter stole my hair!

13:05.854 --> 13:07.440
- Settle down, Jeffrey!
- Justin.

13:07.523 --> 13:11.484
Mike. Clearly the Griffin family
is out of control, but not to fear.

13:11.609 --> 13:15.238
I've tangled with superbeings before.
They can be stopped!

13:15.363 --> 13:20.576
You can't stop us, Mayor West!
We are all-powerful!

13:20.659 --> 13:23.577
Clearly you've let yourselves
become drunk with power.

13:23.702 --> 13:25.580
Silence!

13:25.663 --> 13:28.582
- We demand obedience!
- Or else!

13:28.582 --> 13:32.251
Is that all you can do?
Ow! That kinda hurt!

13:32.334 --> 13:35.588
Is that bleeding?
I guess it's all right. Ouch, though!

13:35.671 --> 13:38.924
Anyone who opposes our demands
will be destroyed!

13:39.008 --> 13:42.677
Our first demand:
You will erect a statue in the town square.

13:42.760 --> 13:46.931
It will depict Blair Warner admitting to
Mrs Garrett that the poem she submitted

13:47.055 --> 13:51.643
for her creative writing class was
plagiarised from a work by Emily Dickinson.

13:51.726 --> 13:54.144
We have spoken! Agh!

13:56.229 --> 13:58.940
That's it! We have to fight fire with fire.

13:59.023 --> 14:03.402
If nuclear refuse gave them superpowers,
it could do the same for me.

14:03.402 --> 14:07.906
Citizens, I'm off to the toxic waste dump!

14:14.578 --> 14:17.163
- Mayor West, you have lymphoma.
- Oh, my!

14:17.288 --> 14:19.874
Probably from rolling around in toxic waste.

14:19.999 --> 14:23.001
- I see.
- What were you trying to prove?

14:23.001 --> 14:26.462
- I was trying to gain superpowers.
- That's just silly.

14:26.546 --> 14:29.465
Silly, yes. Idiotic, yes.

14:33.845 --> 14:38.848
No, no! That's not what Mrs Garrett's
bosom looked like. It looked more like this.

14:38.974 --> 14:41.685
Notice the sun spots
at the top of the right can.

14:41.768 --> 14:45.019
Excuse me. I have a message
from the Quahog hospital.

14:46.354 --> 14:52.942
- I just feel awful about this, Mayor West.
- Yeah. Me, too. Stewie, fluff his pillows.

14:53.026 --> 14:55.737
I'll heat up his soup.

14:55.863 --> 14:58.448
I'll go to China to see if there's a cure.
Nope.

14:58.573 --> 15:03.576
Now, now. The doctor says I'll make
a full recovery. But you learned your lesson.

15:03.660 --> 15:07.205
I can't believe we let those superpowers
go to our heads.

15:07.330 --> 15:10.250
- I feel like such a bastard.
- Me, too.

15:10.333 --> 15:13.378
For now, we'll use our powers
to help you get better.

15:13.461 --> 15:19.214
Thank you. As long as I have Mrs Garrett's
giant rack by my bedside, I'll be all right.

15:19.297 --> 15:22.008
Girls! Girls! Girls!

15:37.437 --> 15:42.442
Hear ye, hear ye. I call to order the
first meeting of the We Hate Broads Club.

15:42.567 --> 15:45.987
- Yeah!
- Cos all you need in life is your best pals.

15:45.987 --> 15:49.741
- Sure! As long as those pals ain't dames!
- O-tay!

15:50.490 --> 15:52.368
What was that?

15:52.452 --> 15:55.370
Hey! We told you guys
to quit snooping around here!

15:55.494 --> 15:58.832
We need to find a story
if I'm ever gonna be a big-time reporter.

15:58.914 --> 16:04.544
All right, make like Siamese twins
and split... and then one of you die.

16:04.669 --> 16:07.880
When do we have the grape juice?
I came for grape juice.

16:10.925 --> 16:13.843
Hey, Quagmire, watch this.

16:14.343 --> 16:16.430
Hey, "kick me"!

16:18.222 --> 16:22.893
We have a new studentjoining us this
morning. Her name is Lois Pewterschmidt.

16:22.893 --> 16:26.354
- Ugh! Just what we need, another girl.
- You said it!

16:27.689 --> 16:31.024
Wow! I'd like to play doctor with her!

16:31.149 --> 16:34.985
And remove her inflamed appendix
before it bursts, causing sepsis.

16:35.110 --> 16:38.531
Giggidy-giggidy-giggidy!

16:39.990 --> 16:42.826
- What you reading?
- The Red Badge of Courage.

16:42.909 --> 16:46.871
I sure wish I could meet a brave fella
like the guy in this book.

16:46.871 --> 16:51.792
- You know, I'm a brave guy, Lois.
- You're not brave enough to laugh at death!

16:51.875 --> 16:53.751
Watch me!

16:53.877 --> 16:57.087
Thanks! Like I don't have
enough trouble fitting in!

16:57.087 --> 16:59.507
You're not brave enough
to take your clothes off!

16:59.590 --> 17:01.382
Way ahead of you. Oh!

17:01.465 --> 17:05.345
I bet you're too chicken
to spend a night at the old Selberg place.

17:06.887 --> 17:10.849
- Cleveland, mind stepping out of the way?
- Oh, sorry.

17:12.642 --> 17:14.726
I ain't chicken to spend the night!

17:14.809 --> 17:17.939
I ain't neither!
To prove it, I'll go up there tonight!

17:18.064 --> 17:20.982
- See you there, pal!
- You can't stay in that house!

17:21.066 --> 17:23.568
Old man Selberg's ghost still haunts it.

17:23.568 --> 17:26.404
Not to mention the myriad
of bacteria and allergens

17:26.487 --> 17:30.448
from years of substandard housekeeping.
It does not augur well for you.

17:30.574 --> 17:34.118
Aw, zip it, egghead.
You with your big words and your...

17:34.202 --> 17:37.037
and your small difficult words.

17:37.121 --> 17:40.249
Wow! Any boy who would
spend the night in that creepy place

17:40.374 --> 17:43.167
sure would be the bravest fella I ever met.

17:43.292 --> 17:45.878
That Lois is some kind of woman.

17:46.002 --> 17:49.632
Yeah. Just thinking about her
makes my testicles want to drop.

17:49.757 --> 17:52.342
Oops, speak of the devil.
Ooh. Make that devils.

17:59.764 --> 18:04.852
Quagmire's team takes the left side of the
house and Peter's team will take the right.

18:04.852 --> 18:07.772
Whoever's alive in the morning
can bury his dead pals.

18:07.897 --> 18:13.109
Do I have a cobweb in my hair?
It feels like I have a cobweb in my hair.

18:18.113 --> 18:21.741
- What was that?
- Michael Winslow from Police Academy.

18:33.209 --> 18:36.754
- This house gives me the creeps.
- Yeah, let's get out of here.

18:36.754 --> 18:39.464
Wait, wait. We can't let those guys win.

18:39.464 --> 18:44.176
- We ought to pretend we're ghosts, see?
- Then we'll scare the other guys out...

18:44.260 --> 18:46.971
We say we spent the night
and everyone thinks

18:47.096 --> 18:50.933
we're the bravest kids in the world.
Especially Lois.

18:51.058 --> 18:53.226
All right!

18:59.272 --> 19:01.484
Hey, I got a great idea!

19:01.567 --> 19:03.860
This'll really scare them. Everybody set?

19:03.985 --> 19:05.444
- Check!
- Check!

19:05.528 --> 19:07.320
Sock it to me!

19:12.117 --> 19:15.869
If we had a teacup, this would be like
playing find the teacup in the bedsheet,

19:15.953 --> 19:17.954
like I do with my Aunt Sophia.

19:28.171 --> 19:30.257
Aaaagh!

19:32.008 --> 19:36.512
My God! Not only are ghosts real,
but their innards are made of children.

19:36.595 --> 19:37.637
It's us!

19:37.762 --> 19:39.848
Whoo-oo-oo!

19:41.390 --> 19:44.518
- That's a nice effect!
- Yeah, that's really scary,

19:44.643 --> 19:47.979
Wait a second. If you're there, and I'm here,

19:48.062 --> 19:51.815
and Istanbul is in this general area,
then who the hell is that?

19:58.488 --> 20:02.157
Ha! Get used to this sight, Diane:
Guys running away from you.

20:02.241 --> 20:05.494
You're so deep in the closet
you're finding Christmas presents.

20:08.829 --> 20:12.459
Remember our story:
We tell Lois we both stayed all night.

20:12.583 --> 20:14.669
And I caught the ghost with my lasso.

20:14.752 --> 20:18.087
I punched him so hard
he ran crying all the way back to hell!

20:18.212 --> 20:21.216
She'll have to believe that.
It hangs together perfectly.

20:21.216 --> 20:25.511
Our top story: Cowardly kids
lay down rubber at the old Selberg place.

20:25.595 --> 20:26.636
Turn that up.

20:26.761 --> 20:29.556
Peter Griffin and Glen Quagmire
were seen bolting

20:29.681 --> 20:33.725
out of the supposedly haunted house
after one half-hour,

20:33.850 --> 20:37.187
leaving only their pride
and twin trails of urine behind them.

20:37.270 --> 20:40.397
Cheese and crackers!
Now Lois'll know everything!

20:40.522 --> 20:42.066
Not if I can help it!

20:44.067 --> 20:46.236
- Newsroom.
- This is Peter Griffin.

20:46.362 --> 20:49.279
Stop saying that stuff
or we'll watch something else!

20:49.363 --> 20:53.034
Today on The View:
Cooties, the silent killer.

20:55.827 --> 20:58.746
Lois, there's something we gotta tell you.

20:58.746 --> 21:02.707
Yeah. We didn't stay in the haunted house.
We're not brave.

21:02.832 --> 21:06.669
- I've decided I don't care about bravery.
- You don't?

21:06.669 --> 21:10.965
No. I realised what I really like is smarts.

21:11.049 --> 21:14.509
Sorry I'm late, darling.
I was checking my stool for blood.

21:14.593 --> 21:19.097
- Mort Goldman!
- He's so clever! Show 'em, Morty!

21:20.847 --> 21:22.934
Whoo-oo-oo!

21:28.979 --> 21:30.147
He got us again!

21:30.230 --> 21:33.484
This just shows that
women are nothing but trouble!

21:33.567 --> 21:36.486
You said it! Let's you and me
swear off 'em for good!

21:36.611 --> 21:37.945
And how!

21:41.199 --> 21:45.160
Quagmire, it seems to me we've each
made another 500 million dollars.

21:45.243 --> 21:49.955
Good thing we swore off women
so we could accumulate this vast wealth.

21:50.038 --> 21:53.375
Watch the ticker. I'll go microwave
a bagel and have sex with it.

21:53.500 --> 21:55.251
Butter's in the fridge!

21:55.252 --> 22:56.252
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru